  "caption": "Reverse-ablation effects with paired bootstrap intervals.",
  "reading_guide": "Each point is removal minus full H-soft, with horizontal two-ended 95% paired AB percentile intervals from 5,000 existing draws. Grey circles mark intervals crossing zero; coloured squares mark intervals excluding zero, with positive effects amber and negative effects blue. Geometry removal changes RMSE by +0.1396 and EF by -8.7049. The RMSE and equal-fold EF endpoints are separate panels. Intervals condition on frozen OOF and prior selection, are exploratory and are not multiplicity-adjusted. Removal uses dependency tags: removing X statistics also removes dependent geometry, so effects are not orthogonal causal attributions. The earlier R-log F0/F3/F3+E1 ladder is retained in companion data and moved out of this image as requested. No fit or bootstrap draw is added.",
